# Oracle feature catalog for the acceptance report (format: see mysql.features).

Connection & security | Login with user / password (O5LOGON, 11g and 12c verifiers) | logs_in_with_user_and_password, auth_crypto::tests::verifier_11g_matches_the_reference_vectors, auth_crypto::tests::verifier_12c_matches_the_reference_vectors, auth_crypto::tests::cbc_padding_always_adds_a_block_on_exact_multiples
Connection & security | TCPS (TLS) with each certificate check, incl. listener TLS renegotiation | tcps_connections_with_each_certificate_check
Connection & security | Native network encryption (SQLNET.ENCRYPTION) | GAP: use TCPS
Connection & security | Proxy authentication (user[target] / ?proxy-user=): the server reports USER = target, PROXY_USER = the connecting user; refused without the grant | proxy_authentication_connects_on_behalf_of_another_user
Connection & security | Kerberos authentication | GAP: not in thin mode (python-oracledb thin lacks it too)

Protocol & encoding | NUMBER / DATE / TIMESTAMP / BINARY_DOUBLE encodings checked against the server's own bytes | server_checks::number_encoding_matches_the_servers_own_bytes, server_checks::dates_timestamps_and_floats_compare_equal_on_the_server
Protocol & encoding | Queries with binds; fetches in rounds | select_with_binds_and_types, many_rows_are_fetched_in_rounds
Protocol & encoding | Request bytes match the reference driver's (golden EXECUTE messages) | exec::tests::execute_of_a_query_matches_the_golden_bytes, exec::tests::execute_of_plsql_with_out_bind_matches_the_golden_bytes
Protocol & encoding | TTC primitives: universal integers, byte strings, incomplete-response handling | buf::tests::universal_integers_round_trip, buf::tests::byte_strings_short_long_and_null, buf::tests::running_out_of_bytes_is_incomplete_not_invalid
Protocol & encoding | Statement classification and bind discovery (literals, comments, := skipped) | stmt::tests::classifies_by_first_keyword, stmt::tests::finds_binds_and_skips_literals_comments_and_assignment
Protocol & encoding | NUMBER / DATE / BINARY_DOUBLE codecs (reference tables, round trips) | value::tests::numbers_encode_like_the_reference_table, value::tests::numbers_round_trip, value::tests::dates_and_doubles_round_trip
Protocol & encoding | DML, commit / rollback, server errors mapped (unique violation names the constraint) | dml_commit_rollback_and_errors, exec::tests::unique_violation_names_the_constraint
Protocol & encoding | Statement cache: a repeated SQL / PL/SQL statement re-executes its parsed cursor (20 per session; no re-parse, no re-describe, defines kept) — server parse counter +24 vs +170 without it for 150 executions | repeated_statements_reuse_their_parsed_cursor
Protocol & encoding | Scrollable cursors: first / last / absolute / relative / next / prior over one open cursor (binds kept, CLOB columns defined), other statements in between; through the driver as shared rows | scrollable_cursor_moves_anywhere_in_the_result, scrollable_cursor_through_the_driver_returns_shared_rows

Types | NUMBER typed by precision/scale (Int / Decimal / Float), BINARY_FLOAT/DOUBLE | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering, backend::tests::values_are_typed_by_their_column
Types | VARCHAR2 / NVARCHAR2 / CHAR / RAW | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering
Types | DATE, TIMESTAMP(n), WITH TIME ZONE (offset), WITH LOCAL TIME ZONE — equal to TO_CHAR | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering, value::tests::timestamp_tz_round_trips_with_offsets_and_day_rollover
Types | INTERVAL YEAR TO MONTH / DAY TO SECOND — equal to TO_CHAR | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering, value::tests::intervals_format_like_to_char
Types | JSON (OSON decoded) — equal to JSON_SERIALIZE | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering, oson::tests::escapes_json_strings, oson::tests::rejects_garbage
Types | VECTOR — equal to VECTOR_SERIALIZE | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering
Types | BOOLEAN | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering
Types | ROWID / UROWID (physical and logical) accepted back by the server | every_column_type_is_typed_and_matches_the_servers_rendering, logical_rowids_of_index_organized_tables_round_trip
Types | CLOB / NCLOB / BLOB read and written, 0 B – 1 MB | clob_and_blob_read_and_write
Types | Nested CURSOR(...) columns: each fetched to the end as a result set (120 rows x their own cursors) | nested_cursor_columns_come_back_as_result_sets
Types | BFILE columns: the server file read through its locator (open / read / close), byte-exact vs the server's length; a missing file is the server's error | bfile_columns_are_read_from_the_server_file
Types | Object types (nested), VARRAY / nested tables (of scalars and objects, with NULLs), XMLType (inline and as a CLOB) in query results; LOB / date / BOOLEAN attributes; mapped onto nested structs | objects_collections_and_xmltype_columns_decode
Types | TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE in a named region: local time, offset at that instant (daylight saving) and IANA region name, computed by the server (region ids from V$TIMEZONE_NAMES); columns and PL/SQL results — beyond python-oracledb thin, which refuses them | timestamps_in_named_regions_come_back_as_the_server_computes_them

ORM (shared layer) | Shared conformance suite (CRUD, values, batch, query builder, binary, unique violation, transactions, row locks, raw SQL, joins/aggregates, execute_many failure semantics, server cursors) | oracle_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Select builder: INNER / LEFT JOIN, WHERE on any joined entity, GROUP BY, COUNT/COUNT DISTINCT/SUM/AVG/MIN/MAX, HAVING, ORDER BY, OFFSET/FETCH, counting groups, entity pairs from a join | oracle_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Results into any struct / tuple by column name (no entity needed), per-field conversion | oracle_conforms

Hand-written SQL | Streaming large results (150k rows); callback errors close the cursor | large_results_stream_and_a_callback_error_stops_cleanly
Hand-written SQL | Array DML (execute_many, 20k rows in one round trip; same outcome as row by row on a failure part-way) | array_dml_runs_many_rows_in_one_call, oracle_conforms
Hand-written SQL | Server-side cursor API: open / fetch batches (FETCH calls) / close, other statements in between, in a transaction | oracle_conforms

PL/SQL | Anonymous blocks, procedures and functions with IN / OUT / IN OUT binds | plsql_blocks_procedures_and_functions
PL/SQL | call(): OUT / IN OUT, REF CURSOR OUT, implicit results (DBMS_SQL.RETURN_RESULT), DBMS_OUTPUT (~700 KB) | procedure_calls_return_out_values_cursors_implicit_results_and_output
PL/SQL | REF CURSORs from procedures and functions | ref_cursors_from_procedures_and_functions
PL/SQL | call_function(), package members, named arguments (any order, skipping defaults) | functions_named_arguments_and_every_out_kind
PL/SQL | OUT of every scalar kind: NUMBER, BINARY_DOUBLE, VARCHAR2, RAW, BOOLEAN, DATE, TIMESTAMP, WITH TIME ZONE, INTERVAL YM / DS, cursor | functions_named_arguments_and_every_out_kind, procedure_calls_return_out_values_cursors_implicit_results_and_output
PL/SQL | Compilation errors reported with line / column / message (not left INVALID silently) | compilation_errors_are_reported_with_their_lines
PL/SQL | Scripts: SQL + PL/SQL units ended by '/', quotes / q'[…]' / comments respected | scripts_run_sql_and_plsql_units_and_stop_at_the_first_error, backend::tests::scripts_split_on_semicolons_and_slash_lines
PL/SQL | Procedure names / parameter names validated (never SQL) | backend::tests::procedure_names_are_identifiers_only, procedure_calls_return_out_values_cursors_implicit_results_and_output
PL/SQL | CLOB / BLOB of any size: OUT arguments and function results read through locators, IN values past 32 KB as temporary LOBs, IN OUT; UTF-16 CLOB data incl. surrogates; temporary LOBs freed (checked in v$temporary_lobs) | out_clob_and_blob_of_any_size_come_back_whole, in_values_past_32k_travel_as_temporary_lobs, in_out_clob_and_blob, lobs_through_call_and_call_function_of_any_size
PL/SQL | Object, collection, RECORD and associative-array (index-by) arguments: IN (pickled, incl. LOB attributes as freed temporary LOBs), OUT, IN OUT and function results — types taken from the procedure declaration (NAME_RESOLVE + ALL_ARGUMENTS) | object_collection_and_record_arguments_through_call

Other Oracle features | Advanced Queuing, Continuous Query Notification, SODA, two-phase commit | GAP: not implemented

Platform & runtime | Runs on Linux: whole live suite against Oracle Database Free, no test skipped (CI) | ci::oracle_live_ubuntu_latest
Platform & runtime | Builds and passes its unit / protocol tests on macOS and Windows (CI; Oracle ships no server for those runners — the sockets are rt-net's, proven live there by the MySQL jobs) | ci::drivers_macos_latest, ci::drivers_windows_latest
Platform & runtime | Fully async on kernway's reactor: DNS and certificate reads on the blocking pool, PBKDF2 login proof there too; no blocking call on a shard — enforced by a source scan | no_blocking_call_runs_on_the_reactor
